t;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">On March 2, 2026, the Company entered into a Master Note and Guaranty Agreement (the &#8220;Senior Note Agreement&#8221;) with NYL Investors LLC and certain of its affiliates </span>(collectively, the &#8220;Purchasers&#8221;)<span style="background:#ffffff;">. The Senior Note Agreement establishes an uncommitted senior unsecured note facility pursuant to which the Company may issue senior unsecured promissory notes (&#8220;Notes&#8221;) from time to time in one or more series to the Purchasers in an aggregate principal amount of up to </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_W8XzfZqNBU-lEpTZLQUYuA" contextRef="As_Of_3_2_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xrn_MasterNoteAndGuarantyAgreementMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_9iZrXW_XlUiKthP0aj8Fjw" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_jgmMV87bFEWPA5EcyjoUbQ">150</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million. The Senior Note Agreement does not obligate the Purchasers to purchase any Notes, and each issuance is subject to the Purchasers&#8217; discretion and satisfaction of customary conditions. Notes may be issued under the Senior Note Agreement during a period ending on the earliest of (i) the third anniversary of the effective date of the Senior Note Agreement, (ii) termination of the facility by either party upon written notice, (iii) termination following certain events of default, or (iv) acceleration of the Notes and termination of the facility. Notes issued under the Senior Note Agreement may have maturities of up to </span><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_3_2_2026_To_3_2_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xrn_MasterNoteAndGuarantyAgreementMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_wBNVCLdu4EaE6UnSBgTXoQ" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentTerm" id="Narr_4oJxVmiitkGpVjsz_rrvvQ"><span style="background:#ffffff;">ten years</span></ix:nonNumeric><span style="background:#ffffff;"> and will bear interest at rates determined at the time of issuance based on spreads over U.S. Treasury securities. As of June 30, 2026, </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_W8XzfZqNBU-lEpTZLQUYuA" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xrn_MasterNoteAndGuarantyAgreementMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_PG6FHswsZU6TW_YQSEDVMw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebt" scale="3" id="Narr_Rgxua8deNEeTQJtTgaQp6Q">no</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> Notes had been issued or were outstanding under the Senior Note Agreement.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Derivative Instruments&#160;- Interest Rate Swaps</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">As of June 30, 2026, the Company had&#160;</span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ef-_kVzx4E6rVyPSxykuTQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_0C_ZdzBgWkWvb3fKCOo2PQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeNumberOfInstrumentsHeld" scale="0" id="Narr_D7Adh8FxF0mZgjx7ZCp5-A">11</ix:nonFraction> <span style="background:#ffffff;">interest rate swaps outstanding that are used to manage its interest rate risk by fixing the SOFR component of its term loans through their maturities, </span>consisting of four interest rate swaps related to Term Loan B and seven interest rate swaps related to the Term Loan A Tranches. The <span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_aNkQejntjkKlFd_5_7mNlQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanBMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_-DdybLtQFU-VVd3FBzJA9A" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:DerivativeNumberOfInstrumentsHeld" scale="0" id="Narr_JEtcTLVCTkmhfpD2P8z2eA">four</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;">&#160;interest rate swaps related to Term Loan B have a combined notional value of </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$</span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_W8XzfZqNBU-lEpTZLQUYuA" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanBMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_-DdybLtQFU-VVd3FBzJA9A" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeNotionalAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_r-viCb4ZC0KMpANvBBrZnA">150</ix:nonFraction><span style="background:#ffffff;">&#160;million and fix the&#160;SOFR&#160;component on Term Loan B through January 2028 at&#160;</span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ef-_kVzx4E6rVyPSxykuTQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanBMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_-DdybLtQFU-VVd3FBzJA9A" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeFixedInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_dS0bTGzHg0Sjob7-YkkjkQ">2.54</ix:nonFraction>%<span style="background:#ffffff;">. The </span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_aNkQejntjkKlFd_5_7mNlQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanOneMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_W7aJYM-qBEyTecMn2zJiTg" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:DerivativeNumberOfInstrumentsHeld" scale="0" id="Narr_Ok11xaxUW0G79YOtbUz2Qg">seven</ix:nonFraction><span style="background:#ffffff;"> interest rate swaps related to the Term Loan A Tranches have a combined notional value of </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_W8XzfZqNBU-lEpTZLQUYuA" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanOneMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_W7aJYM-qBEyTecMn2zJiTg" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeNotionalAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_1Zlnt4edlk-ywL1YmbwNCw">350</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million and fix the SOFR components on the Term Loan A Tranches at rates between </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ef-_kVzx4E6rVyPSxykuTQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanOneMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_c7Ve-EfzLESPx5R-pgWqZg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeFixedInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_GkRwU_isa0qDy2kz1SIxSg">3.24</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> to </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ef-_kVzx4E6rVyPSxykuTQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_xrn_TermLoanOneMember_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_wnQME1S17k6X7Fz9ITmUkw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeFixedInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_g22xTU1UckOXJawRqckmIg">3.32</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> and have maturities in October 2029, October 2030, and April 2031.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:12pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">The Company records the swaps either as an asset or a liability measured at its fair value at each reporting period. When hedge accounting is applied, the change in the fair value of derivatives designated and that qualify as cash flow hedges is (i)&#160;recorded in accumulated other comprehensive income in the equity section of the Company&#8217;s Condensed Consolidated Balance Sheets and </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">-18-</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="_4ec052da_4773_4e66_8556_49e9df593037"></a><a id="Tc_ygzVUJNoS0CdF2wapffTdw_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_YPDf3cxeH06mUkFCUGa54Q_1_8"></a><a id="Tc_YIFvUZhFl0mMJNNEmrnfUQ_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_YUQFjfpt7UO_5VRYwgw0LQ_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_EohUk-Tdt0qTPjXqDCaVog_2_8"></a><a id="Tc_-PlCDMWTGU-jEHVeXqEv2g_2_11"></a><a id="Tc_ntWewRGJD0KcMmE7al1s4g_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_1k_T6gADPUOqJP7To9PAgw_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_Kw-rbOVfCUigP_2uJX82dQ_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_2daT7fwZT06kOmG77mliZg_3_8"></a><a id="Tc_LzQZDO2knUSx4UR2ifjmdw_3_11"></a><a id="Tc_GaiQSGB7XE2Ka4ckSlSOtA_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_HnIjqdYiI0aCGBj9XRHq3g_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_kLBhLB6Sn06adO227a0Wkw_5_2"></a><a id="Tc_znKBiP0bAE60Hn651DDJHQ_5_5"></a><a id="Tc_4mReO6oP20SSmqrNhM_WWA_5_8"></a><a id="Tc_y3nxtqo7mk-QrJbq20gwvg_5_11"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_ORxjtAf2EUCqoVjG4JXsiw_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">(ii)&#160;subsequently reclassified into earnings as interest expense for the period that the hedged forecasted transactions affect earnings. If specific hedge accounting criteria are not met, changes in the Company&#8217;s derivative instruments&#8217; fair value are recognized currently as an adjustment to net income. As of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, all of the Company&#8217;s swaps met the criteria for hedge accounting.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="color:#ee0000;visibility:hidden;background:#ffff00;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company&#8217;s interest rate swaps are not traded on an exchange. The Company&#8217;s interest rate swaps are recorded at fair value based on a variety of observable inputs including contractual terms, interest rate curves, yield curves, measure of volatility, and correlations of such inputs. The Company measures its derivatives at fair value on a recurring basis based on the expected size of future cash flows on a discounted basis and incorporates a measure of non-performance risk. The fair values are based on Level 2 inputs within the framework of ASC Topic 820. The Company considers its own credit risk, as well as the credit risk of its counterparties, when evaluating the fair value of its derivative instruments.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The fair value of the Company&#8217;s interest rate swaps was an asset of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_W8XzfZqNBU-lEpTZLQUYuA" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_0C_ZdzBgWkWvb3fKCOo2PQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeAssets" scale="3" id="Narr_HtxSsEQ9l02nrdH_NObo4g">10,898</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_W8XzfZqNBU-lEpTZLQUYuA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_DerivativeInstrumentRiskAxis_us-gaap_InterestRateSwapMember_WXXjnrrBzU2ddeq96ijaoQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeAssets" scale="3" id="Narr_zPk7Asc7okmkMfYOJ0BVEA">6,102</ix:nonFraction> as of June 30, 2026 and December&#160;31,&#160;2025, respectively. The balances are included in the &#8220;Derivative Assets&#8221; line item on the Company&#8217;